 Axolot v0.11 uses Microsoft Device Code OAuth. Register Axolot as your own public/native Microsoft application, enable public client flows, and paste the application's Client ID in **Settings → Microsoft App Client ID**. The launcher never asks for a Microsoft password or client secret. The login chain is Microsoft OAuth → Xbox Live → XSTS → Minecraft Services → ownership/profile verification.
 
 ### Automatic updates
-Axolot checks `https://github.com/DiskiiVn/Craftopia-bot/releases/latest/download/axolot-update.json` at startup. The release workflow builds the NSIS installer, calculates SHA-256, publishes the installer + manifest to GitHub Releases, and the launcher downloads/verifies/installs the new version silently. Users do not need to manually download a new installer.
+Axolot checks the Supabase stable update channel at startup. The release workflow builds the NSIS installer, calculates SHA-256, publishes the installer + manifest to GitHub Releases, and the launcher downloads/verifies/installs the new version silently. Users do not need to manually download a new installer.
 
 
 ## v0.12.0 cloud-managed configuration
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@ Admin portal: `https://axolot-client-updates-pter.vercel.app`
 - The launcher does not reuse another launcher's Client ID and does not attempt to bypass Minecraft Services authorization.
 
 
-## v0.12.4 Multi Identity Vault
+## v0.12.5 Multi Identity Vault
 - Unlimited Offline/Crack identities with single-add and bulk-add support.
 - Multiple Microsoft/Premium identities can coexist in the same launcher.
 - Microsoft refresh tokens are stored in the OS credential vault via the Rust keyring backend, never in localStorage.
@@ -61,10 +61,20 @@ Admin portal: `https://axolot-client-updates-pter.vercel.app`
 - Minecraft AppID approval handling from v0.12.1 remains in place.
 
 
-## v0.12.4 Fixed Desktop Shell + Hands-free Update
+## v0.12.5 Fixed Desktop Shell + Hands-free Update
 - Play is now a fixed desktop dashboard: no full-window page scrolling and no marketing-style hero copy.
 - Navigation is a compact icon rail on the left; only content-heavy views such as Profiles, Mods, Accounts and Settings scroll inside their own panels.
 - The launch control is icon-first and no longer displays “Play Minecraft”.
 - Automatic updates are enabled by default. On startup Axolot checks the signed release channel, downloads the NSIS installer internally, verifies SHA-256, starts the silent installer, then exits the old build.
 - Background update checks run when the launcher regains focus and every 10 minutes. If Minecraft is currently running, Axolot defers installation instead of interrupting the session.
 - GitHub Actions builds the Windows NSIS installer and publishes `axolot-update.json` automatically for `axolot-v*` tags.
+
+
+## v0.13.0 Fast-inspired unified client
+- Uses one consistent desktop geometry across Play, Profiles, Mods, Accounts, Client and Settings.
+- Sidebar expands on hover without shifting the app; the main window remains resizable/maximizable.
+- Adds a first-class Mods dashboard and Axolot Core dashboard instead of placeholder Partners/Store pages.
+- Axolot Core is built from the user-provided Fast Client source, visibly rebranded and recolored for the Axolot Nebula design system.
+- Core 0.13.0 targets Fabric 1.21.4 in this release; other profile versions are kept compatible by not injecting the Core JAR.
+- AutoBoost continues to install Sodium/Lithium/FerriteCore/ImmediatelyFast/EntityCulling and only adds Axolot Core when the profile is compatible.
+- Release builds compile Axolot Core first, embed the exact JAR into the launcher, build the NSIS installer, hash it and publish the update manifest.
